@startuml
title Automatic browser connection across desktop platforms
actor Learner
participant Settings
participant Runtime
participant "OS permission prompt" as Permission
participant "Settings guardian" as Guardian
database "Owned settings journal" as Journal
participant Browser
participant "Stable local proxy" as Proxy
Learner -> Settings: Allow website blocking and connection changes
Settings -> Runtime: Enable automatic connection
Runtime -> Proxy: Start stable loopback endpoint with fresh proof
alt Linux or macOS
  Runtime -> Permission: Request administrator-authorized guardian
  Permission -> Guardian: Start after approval
  Guardian -> Runtime: Authenticate over loopback control socket
else Windows
  Runtime -> Guardian: Start per-user guardian
end
Guardian -> Journal: Recover owned settings; record prior values
Guardian -> Browser: Apply persistent policies / system PAC
Guardian --> Runtime: Settings applied (not routing proof)
Browser -> Proxy: Connection verification
Proxy --> Runtime: Browser routing observed
Runtime --> Settings: Connection checked; check each browser separately
Learner -> Browser: Close and reopen normally
Browser -> Proxy: Requests use persistent routing without launch flags
Runtime -> Proxy: Evaluate current focus state and rules
loop While application is alive
  Runtime -> Guardian: Heartbeat
  Guardian --> Runtime: Owned settings unchanged
end
alt Disable, disconnect or parent death
  Guardian -> Browser: Restore only still-owned settings
  Guardian -> Journal: Confirm restoration
  Runtime -> Proxy: Stop forwarding
else User replaces settings
  Guardian -> Browser: Preserve replacement; restore other owned policies
  Guardian --> Runtime: Configuration changed
end
@enduml
